cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite this software record for the OfftargetPred web interface and the CRISPert
  paper in references for the base method. Record the actual commit
  and model hashes used in your analysis. No software DOI has been assigned.
type: software
title: "CRISPert web server: a web interface to sequence-only CRISPert-small models"
authors:
  - name: OfftargetPred contributors
repository-code: https://github.com/Alexander-Mitrofanov/OfftargetPred-web-server
url: https://alexander-mitrofanov.github.io/OfftargetPred-web-server/
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-19
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Web interface for scoring aligned CRISPR guide/candidate sequence pairs and
  bounded candidate discovery using three supplied, unchanged sequence-only
  CRISPert-small checkpoints. Outputs are uncalibrated model scores. MIT applies
  only to project-owned code and documentation; third-party components and the
  supplied tokenizer, weights, datasets, and publications are excluded.
  Upstream tokenizer, weight, and dataset redistribution permissions are
  unverified. See LICENSE, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and docs/licensing.md.
keywords:
  - CRISPR
  - off-target prediction
  - CRISPert
  - web interface
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "CRISPert: A Transformer-Based Model for CRISPR-Cas Off-Target Prediction"
    authors:
      - family-names: Jobson Pargeter
        given-names: William
      - family-names: Backofen
        given-names: Rolf
      - family-names: Tran
        given-names: Van Dinh
    year: 2024
    collection-title: "Machine Learning and Knowledge Discovery in Databases. Research Track"
    start: 92
    end: 104
    doi: 10.1007/978-3-031-70368-3_6
    url: https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-70368-3_6
